<h3>Spanner</h3>
<p><i>2015 - present</i></p>
<p>
Spanner is one of my largest projects. It is an event and membership management system for Land Rover owner clubs.
</p>
<p>
It has gone through many iterations, including a simplified but complete <a href="https://github.com/archey347/Spanner">Visual
Basic version for an A-level coursework</a>. The most recent iteration (v3) is very modular and is designed such that it could be
used for other types organisations in theory, but it hasn't been practiced.
</p>
<p>
The name was inspired by the name of Scout's membership system at the time, compass.
</p>
<p>
<a href="https://spanner.wwlrc.co.uk/">https://spanner.wwlrc.co.uk</a>
</p>

<h3>Wye &amp; Welsh Land Rover Club Website</h3>
<p><i>2014 - present</i></p>
<p>
A website for a land rover club. One of my first projects that had was used by acutal
people (which for teen year-old me was a big deal). The current iteration is a <a href="https://github.com/wwlrc/website">nextjs static
build</a>, pulling dynamic data like events and blog posts from spanner (see above).
</p>
<p>
The first iteration was made with <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebPlus">Serif WebPlus</a> and some custom PHP
bodged on to allow committee to manage the blog posts and the calendar. The second iteration was built with
<a href="https://www.wysiwygwebbuilder.com/">WYSIWYG Web Builder</a>
and included an even greater set of bodges to get it to work with
<a href="https://userfrosting.com">UserFrosting</a>.
</p>
<p>
<a href="https://wwlrc.co.uk/">https://wwlrc.co.uk</a>
</p>

<h3>Ray Tracer</h3>
<p><i>Autumn 2023</i></p>
<p>
A project for an Adanced Computer Graphics module final year module at University (one of my most favourite modules), taught by <a href="https://researchportal.bath.ac.uk/en/persons/ken-cameron">Ken Cameron</a>. Features included shadows, reflections, transparency and motion blur (including rolling shutter).
</p>
<p>
We had to submit the code and a report, and the week after a final image that would demonstrate the functions of our ray tracer. I can't share the code
for the project, to stop future students copying, but I can share the final image.
</p>
<p>
Unfortunutly I discovered a memory leak in my ray tracer the week before the final image was due in, which hindered the quality of the final picture I could produce (generating
it used all 64GB of memory in my laptop!). Otherwise I would've been able to use a greater number of samples for the motion blur, and produced longer
star streaks.
</p>
<p>
One day I might revisit it to try and hunt out that memory leak.
</p>
<p>
<img src="/media/image.png" alt="Final ray traced image" width="600">
</p>

<h3>Visualisation of a Four Stroke Internal Combusion Engine</h3>
<p><i>Autumn 2021</i></p>
<p>
Graphical visualisation of a four stroke internal combustion engine. I made it as part of a coursework for a graphics unit whilst at uni.
</p>
<p>
Allows customisation of the amount of pistons and their timings, by entering a set of degree offsets (0 to 720 degrees), deliminated by commas.
</p>
<p>
<a target="_blank" href="https://scrapbook.archbar.me/graphics/engine.html">Visit</a>
</p>

<h3>Diary Generator</h3>
<p><i>September 2018</i></p>
<p>
My family always have a paper diary to keep track of who is doing what. Unlike a traditional
calendar, it has a column for each person, and an extra for birthdays.
</p>
<p>
To create this diary, my mum had a set of seven word documents with a pre-filled in table with all the dates for each day of the week. So if
you had a month that started on a Tuesday, you could select the Tuesday word document, update
the title and adjust the number of days in the month to suit.
</p>
<p>
The task of printing of a new diary each year often got delegated to me. I found using the above
system quite repetative, so I ended up coding a solution instead.
</p>
<p>
<a href="https://scrapbook.archbar.me/diary-generator/diary.php">https://scrapbook.archbar.me/diary-generator/diary.php</a><br>
<a href="https://github.com/archey347/diary-generator/">https://github.com/archey347/diary-generator/</a>
</p>
